BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:10 Days in a Madhouse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T133000
UID:cb25416e41e72c88db60fe9e73757346@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Is she insane\, or just pretending? In this gripping psycholog
 ical opera based on true events from 1887\, trailblazing reporter Nellie B
 ly fakes madness to expose the truth from inside New York's notorious Blac
 kwell's Asylum. What she discovers is a world where women are silenced\, s
 anity is questioned\, and power decides who is believed. This Canadian pre
 miere from composer Rene Orth and librettist Hannah Moscovitch stars Mirei
 lle Asselin as Nellie Bly and Jorell Williams as Dr. Blackwell. Directed b
 y Joanna Settle (Sky on Swings)\, 10 Days in a Madhouse boasts an evocativ
 e set by Andrew Lieberman that transforms the asylum into a maze of the mi
 nd. Composed by Rene Orth with a libretto by Hannah Moscovitch\, 10 Days i
 n a Madhouse is directed by Joanna Settle (Sky on Swings). Designer Andrew
  Lieberman's set transforms the asylum into a maze of the mind.
LOCATION:Bluma Appel Theatre\, 27 Front St E\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://am.ticketmaster.com/tolive/10daysinamadhouse-lum2026
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South by South East International Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T120000
UID:6739ab79dbdb6b18297e474430269068@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Watch as we transform Nathan Phillips Square into a high-energ
 y\, global playground and celebrate Toronto's "World in a City" identity. 
 Tap into your latin flare with open-air dance floor with top Latin DJs\, s
 alsa\, bachata and dance workshops and show-stopping Latin dance performan
 ces\, thunderous drumming ensembles and live salsa big bands and Latin orc
 hestras. Be dazzled by Chinese lion and fan dances and K-Pop and Bollywood
  showcases. Enjoy acrobatics\, samba\, mariachi and feast on our interatio
 nal market\, cuisine\, food truck alley and shopping. Watch live matches o
 f soccer's biggest event! Perfect for the whole family\, this isn't just a
  festival\, it's a full-on cultural explosion in the heart of the city.
LOCATION:Nathan Phillips Square\, 100 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/south-by-south-east-international-festival
